# Microsoft Teams "Incoming Webhook" URLs for the C group (task creators),
# one per line. Every URL here gets pinged on two events, regardless of
# which creator owns the task:
#   - a worker claims a task
#   - a worker marks a task done (submits it for review)
#
# How to add one:
#   1. In Microsoft Teams, open the channel or chat where creators should
#      see these pings (a "Task Bidder - Creators" channel works well if you
#      want everyone in one place).
#   2. Channel menu (...) -> Connectors -> Incoming Webhook -> Configure.
#   3. Give it a name and copy the generated URL.
#   4. Paste that URL on its own line below.
#
# Maintained directly by admins by editing this file on the server - not
# exposed through the web UI. Copy this file to teams_webhooks_creators.txt
# (drop the .example) and fill in real URLs; that file is gitignored since
# each URL can post into that channel on its own (treat it like a secret).
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. This is a separate
# list from teams_webhooks.txt (which only covers new-task notifications).
